    "url": "https://developer.atlassian.com/cloud/jira/platform/webhooks/",
    "retrieved": "2026-09-10",
    "evidence": "composed",
    "note": "Atlassian documents the envelope (timestamp, webhookEvent, issue_event_type_name, user, issue, comment), states that `issue` is \"the same shape returned from the Jira REST API when an issue is retrieved with NO expand parameters\" and that the comment \"is the same shape returned from the Jira REST API when a comment is retrieved\" — but publishes no complete comment_created example. This file is those documented parts assembled, and the normaliser reports `malformed_payload` when a comment event arrives without an issue rather than guessing. The `user` has no emailAddress because the documented webhook user shape omits it. Headers are the documented ones: X-Atlassian-Webhook-Identifier (\"unique within a Jira Cloud tenant and is the same across retries\"), X-Atlassian-Webhook-Flow, and X-Hub-Signature, which the replay harness computes over the exact bytes it sends — a signature literal here would be a signature over a body nobody can reproduce."
  },
